Subject: [PATCH] media: sc4336p: keep the native flip for VFLIP = 0

The init table writes 0x3221 = 0x66 (flip + mirror), the upright
picture on the Wuuk Y0510; the vendor driver leaves those bits alone for
vflip = 0. The VFLIP control defaults to 0 and is applied at stream on,
where it cleared the flip bits (0x3221 = 0x06), so the picture came out
upside down although timps has image.vflip = 0.

Treat the init value as the native orientation: VFLIP = 1 clears the
flip bits, VFLIP = 0 keeps them. Mirror bits (0x06) stay untouched.

Seen on a Wuuk Y0510 (T31X): with 0x3221 = 0x66 the picture is upright.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/sc4336p.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/sc4336p.c
@@ -612,9 +612,14 @@
 				(vts >> 8) & 0xff, &ret);
 		break;
 	case V4L2_CID_VFLIP:
+		/*
+		 * The init table sets 0x3221 = 0x66 (flip + mirror), which is
+		 * the upright picture on the Wuuk Y0510 and what the vendor driver
+		 * keeps for vflip = 0, so VFLIP = 1 clears the flip bits.
+		 */
 		ret = cci_update_bits(sc4336p->regmap, SC4336P_REG_FLIP,
 				      SC4336P_FLIP_MASK,
-				      ctrl->val ? SC4336P_FLIP_MASK : 0, NULL);
+				      ctrl->val ? 0 : SC4336P_FLIP_MASK, NULL);
 		break;
 	default:
 		ret = -EINVAL;
